  "result": {
    "summary": "Deterministic/shadow behavior matches the spec and all listed acceptance tests are present, but the active-mode recovery ladder in spawn.py's review path violates the module's own documented invariant ('previously posted review verdicts still take precedence over an unparseable final response') by running contracts.process before the existing-result guard.",
    "verdict": "request_changes",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/spawn.py",
        "line": 1359,
        "issue": "In the review/spec_review branch, `result = contracts.process(task_id, role, result, cfg=pool.cfg, session=repair_session)` runs before `parse_failed`/`existing_result` are computed (lines 1367-1370). When contracts.mode is 'active' and the worker already posted a valid verdict mid-run via bus_post_result but ends with an unparseable/verdict-less final response, contracts.process will call recover(), which resumes the same Claude session (repair_session) and may return a repaired result containing a *new* verdict. That makes `result.get('verdict')` truthy, so `parse_failed` becomes False and execution falls into the final `else` branch, posting the freshly recovered (possibly different) verdict and silently overwriting the already-posted one \u2014 exactly the T-0139 regression the adjacent comment and existing_result guard were written to prevent, and exactly what docs/hermes-hardening/13-output-contracts.md claims is preserved ('Previously posted review verdicts still take precedence over an unparseable final response'). No test in this diff exercises 'existing_result has a verdict' together with contracts.mode=active, so the regression is untested.",
        "severity": "high"
      }
    ],
